From: PupJune2 <PupJune2@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 13:00:00 +0000
Subject: CromIKO Download Manager

Add the CromIKO download manager, with its settings in Settings >
Downloads > CromIKO download manager (with the mascot):

- Connections per file: 1, 2, 3, 4 (the default), 6 or 8. Chromium
  already downloads big files over several connections with HTTP range
  requests when the server allows it; this sets how many.
- Downloads at the same time: 1 to 5 (3 by default) or no limit. The
  newer downloads wait in a queue and start when an older one ends.
  The queue survives a restart.
- Wi-Fi only: downloads wait while the phone uses mobile data (or a
  metered network) and continue on Wi-Fi.
- Sort into folders: new files go to Download/CromIKO/Videos, Music,
  Pictures, Documents, Apps or Archives (off by default).

A waiting download says "In queue" or "Waiting for Wi-Fi" in its
notification and in the download list. Resuming it (the notification
button says "Start now") runs it right away, whatever the limit and
the network are; so does resuming a download the user paused.
Downloads that could not continue after waiting (no ETag or
Last-Modified) and downloads still waiting for a decision of the user
(location, danger warnings) never wait in the queue.

Running downloads show their speed in the notification, and speed and
connections in the download list, next to the time left. Pausing,
resuming and the automatic retry after a network loss are Chromium's.

The queue is chrome/browser/download/cromiko_download_queue.cc, owned
by ChromeDownloadManagerDelegate; tools/cromiko/download-test tests it.

